cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Non-Orientable UV Unwrapping: Seamless Texture Parameterization"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-01-22
url: "https://github.com/MacMayo1993/SEAM-UV-Mapping"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MacMayo1993/SEAM-UV-Mapping"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "MacMayo"
    given-names: "1993"
    alias: "MacMayo1993"
keywords:
  - "UV mapping"
  - "mesh parameterization"
  - "non-orientable topology"
  - "computer graphics"
  - "Blender"
  - "seamless textures"
abstract: |
  A novel UV parameterization method that eliminates visible texture seams
  by representing surface coordinates on non-orientable quotient domains.
  Instead of cutting closed surfaces to create planar UV maps, this approach
  uses orientation parity tracking and antipodal identification to achieve
  seamless texture sampling. The method achieves 15-20% less distortion than
  traditional methods while eliminating all visible seams under texture filtering.
